license: "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0"
version: "2026.2"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
abstract: >
  ATHENA is a reception-analysis framework for narrative influence. Its four
  poles (narrative structure, audience configuration, psychological reactance,
  activation dynamics) are fed by upstream layers (archetypal reading,
  attacker-side frameworks such as DISARM and DIMA, reception substrate) and
  an explicit objective-setting stage, within a human-in-the-loop,
  LLM-assisted analytical chain governed by an evidence contract on inputs
  and declared proof regimes on outputs.
keywords:
  - narrative analysis
  - psychological reactance
  - strategic communication
  - disinformation analysis
  - influence analysis
  - information dynamics
  - narrative reception
  - FIMI
  - archetypes
